Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables & columns  
• `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt` – the only table that holds yearly debt figures.  
  – `country_code`: filter rows for Russia (`'RUS'`).  
  – `country_name`: alternate filter (`'Russian Federation'`).  
  – `indicator_name` / `indicator_code`: identify each debt series.  
  – `value`: the debt amount we will compare.  
  – `year`: lets us pick specific years or aggregate (MAX / AVG) over time.

Typical filter conditions  
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'  
  ‒ or ‒  
WHERE LOWER(country_name) = 'russian federation'  

10 sample‑to‑solution BigQuery SQL queries
```sql
-- 1) Quick glance at the raw debt table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Make sure we know the exact country name that refers to Russia
SELECT DISTINCT country_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE LOWER(country_name) LIKE '%russ%'
ORDER BY country_name;
```

```sql
-- 3) List every debt‑related indicator that exists for Russia
SELECT DISTINCT indicator_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
ORDER BY indicator_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Inspect one specific indicator (example) through time
SELECT year, value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
  AND indicator_code = 'DT.DOD.DECT.CD'        -- external debt stocks, total (current US$)
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) For each indicator, find the single highest value ever recorded for Russia
SELECT
  indicator_name,
  indicator_code,
  MAX(value) AS max_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
GROUP BY indicator_name, indicator_code
ORDER BY max_value DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Fetch the TOP‑3 debt indicators by that maximum value
SELECT
  indicator_name,
  indicator_code,
  MAX(value) AS max_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
GROUP BY indicator_name, indicator_code
ORDER BY max_value DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

```sql
-- 7) See every yearly observation for those TOP‑3 indicators
WITH top3 AS (
  SELECT indicator_code
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
  WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
  GROUP BY indicator_code
  ORDER BY MAX(value) DESC
  LIMIT 3
)
SELECT
  t.indicator_name,
  t.indicator_code,
  t.year,
  t.value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt` AS t
JOIN top3 USING (indicator_code)
WHERE t.country_code = 'RUS'
ORDER BY t.indicator_code, t.year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) (Optional) Average debt levels in the 2010‑2020 period for extra insight
SELECT
  indicator_name,
  indicator_code,
  AVG(value) AS avg_value_2010_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
  AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2020
GROUP BY indicator_name, indicator_code
ORDER BY avg_value_2010_2020 DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same TOP‑3 result using a window function
SELECT
  indicator_name,
  indicator_code,
  max_value
FROM (
  SELECT
    indicator_name,
    indicator_code,
    MAX(value) AS max_value,
    RANK() OVER (ORDER BY MAX(value) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
  WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
  GROUP BY indicator_name, indicator_code
)
WHERE rnk <= 3
ORDER BY max_value DESC;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: names & peak amounts of the three largest debt indicators for Russia
SELECT
  indicator_name,
  MAX(value) AS highest_recorded_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_intl_debt.international_debt`
WHERE country_code = 'RUS'
GROUP BY indicator_name
ORDER BY highest_recorded_value DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

